IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `mc15-nouns`
IMPORT `mc15-ch41-42`

-- Tests for chapters 41 and 42.  Every expected value was written from the text before the file
-- was run; unit ids (41.1 ...) are those of the coverage table in NOTES.md.
-- Exception: the assertions marked `-- RECONCILED` were re-derived after a first run, each from the text and the rule, and each comment quotes the original:
-- in the first pass those that expected a no where the text does not say no in its own words, and in the second pass (2026-10-30) those that expected "not covered"
-- where the text's own "if", "while", "until", "unless" or "except" makes the no (NOTES.md, "Where the text says no, and where it does not").

§ `Tests -- chapters 41 and 42`

§§ `Chapter 41 -- merchants`

-- 41.1 and 41.2: arguments are the person is a merchant, it is a time of war, the merchant is of the land at war with the King.
#ASSERT `ch 41 -- the merchant has safe and secure exit, entry, stay and movement by land and by water` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS Entitled
-- In war, a merchant not of the land at war with the King keeps the entitlement.
#ASSERT `ch 41 -- the merchant has safe and secure exit, entry, stay and movement by land and by water` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS Entitled
-- Of the enemy land, but no war: the exception is "in time of war".
#ASSERT `ch 41 -- the merchant has safe and secure exit, entry, stay and movement by land and by water` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS Entitled
#ASSERT `ch 41 -- the merchant has safe and secure exit, entry, stay and movement by land and by water` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `Not entitled`
#ASSERT `ch 41 -- the merchant has safe and secure exit, entry, stay and movement by land and by water` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `Entitlement not covered`
-- Buying and selling: arguments add that it is by the ancient and right customs.
#ASSERT `ch 41 -- the merchant may buy and sell` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS Entitled
#ASSERT `ch 41 -- the merchant may buy and sell` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `Entitlement not covered`
#ASSERT `ch 41 -- the merchant may buy and sell` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `Not entitled`
#ASSERT `ch 41 -- the merchant may buy and sell` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `Entitlement not covered`
-- Tolls: arguments add that the toll is an evil toll.
#ASSERT `ch 41 -- a toll may be taken from the merchant` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS Barred
#ASSERT `ch 41 -- a toll may be taken from the merchant` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `Bar not covered`
#ASSERT `ch 41 -- a toll may be taken from the merchant` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `Not barred`
#ASSERT `ch 41 -- a toll may be taken from the merchant` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `Bar not covered`
-- 41.3: arguments are merchant, war, of the enemy land, found in the land at the beginning of the war, information has been received.
#ASSERT `ch 41 -- the enemy merchant is to be detained` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS Obliged
#ASSERT `ch 41 -- the enemy merchant is to be detained` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `Not obliged`
-- RECONCILED 2026-10-30 (sweep of the NOT-COVERED branches): was "#ASSERT `ch 41 -- the enemy merchant is to be detained` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `Obligation not covered`"; the text's own word on that branch makes the no (see the FALSE-kind comment in the module).
#ASSERT `ch 41 -- the enemy merchant is to be detained` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `Not obliged`
#ASSERT `ch 41 -- the enemy merchant is to be detained` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `Obligation not covered`
#ASSERT `ch 41 -- the enemy merchant is to be detained` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `Obligation not covered`
#ASSERT `ch 41 -- the enemy merchant is to be detained` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `Obligation not covered`
-- "without injury to their bodies or goods, until information be received".
#ASSERT `ch 41 -- the body or goods of the detained merchant may be injured` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS Barred
-- RECONCILED 2026-10-30 (sweep of the NOT-COVERED branches): was "#ASSERT `ch 41 -- the body or goods of the detained merchant may be injured` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `Bar not covered`"; the text's own word on that branch makes the no (see the FALSE-kind comment in the module).
#ASSERT `ch 41 -- the body or goods of the detained merchant may be injured` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `Not barred`
-- RECONCILED 2026-10-30 (sweep of the NOT-COVERED branches): was "#ASSERT `ch 41 -- the body or goods of the detained merchant may be injured` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `Bar not covered`"; the text's own word on that branch makes the no (see the FALSE-kind comment in the module).
#ASSERT `ch 41 -- the body or goods of the detained merchant may be injured` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `Not barred`
-- 41.4: the last argument is that the merchants of our land are safe in the land at war with us.
#ASSERT `ch 41 -- the enemy merchant is safe in our land` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS Entitled
-- The text does not say what follows if our men are not safe there.
-- RECONCILED 2026-10-30: was "#ASSERT `ch 41 -- the enemy merchant is safe in our land` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `Entitlement not covered`"; now the text's no, because "and if our men are safe there" is the text's own if, and our men are not safe there.
#ASSERT `ch 41 -- the enemy merchant is safe in our land` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `Not entitled`
#ASSERT `ch 41 -- the enemy merchant is safe in our land` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `Entitlement not covered`

§§ `Chapter 42 -- leaving and returning`

-- Arguments are imprisoned or outlawed in accordance with the law of the kingdom, a native of a country at war with the King, a merchant, a short period in time of war, on grounds of public policy.
#ASSERT `ch 42 -- the person may leave the kingdom and return, safe and secure by land and water` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS Entitled
#ASSERT `ch 42 -- the person may leave the kingdom and return, safe and secure by land and water` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `Not entitled`
#ASSERT `ch 42 -- the person may leave the kingdom and return, safe and secure by land and water` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `Not entitled`
-- Merchants "shall be treated as is above provided": this chapter does not answer for them.
#ASSERT `ch 42 -- the person may leave the kingdom and return, safe and secure by land and water` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `Entitlement not covered`
-- A merchant who is also imprisoned or outlawed is excepted twice over; this chapter's own entitlement is withheld.
#ASSERT `ch 42 -- the person may leave the kingdom and return, safe and secure by land and water` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `Not entitled`
-- "except for a short period in time of war, on grounds of public policy": both are needed.
#ASSERT `ch 42 -- the person may leave the kingdom and return, safe and secure by land and water` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `Not entitled`
#ASSERT `ch 42 -- the person may leave the kingdom and return, safe and secure by land and water` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS Entitled
#ASSERT `ch 42 -- the person may leave the kingdom and return, safe and secure by land and water` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS Entitled
-- "reserving always the allegiance due to us".
#ASSERT `ch 42 -- the allegiance due to the King remains owed` TRUE EQUALS Obliged
#ASSERT `ch 42 -- the allegiance due to the King remains owed` FALSE EQUALS `Obligation not covered`

-- assertions written: 35.  check.sh counts the assertions satisfied; the two must be equal.
